  <section class="card full">
    <span class="mini">Daphne's synthesis</span>
    <h2>My own cleaned-up rule of thumb</h2>
    <p>Start with the smallest project that solves your problem. If it is a personal assistant on your own machine, NanoClaw or OpenClaw. If it is a Pi project, PicoClaw. If you are researching safety for a team, NemoClaw. Give the agent the minimum access needed for day one, and only expand after the first little harbor is working well.</p>
    <p>This is what keeps surfacing across every conversation: people who go wide too fast get burned; people who start narrow and grow carefully are the ones still posting good reviews six months later.</p>
  </section>
